    300  f0fc							; --- E4 moth body (bank2 free space $F008-$F9D8) -------------------------
    301  f0fc							; Entered from bank0 via the $FEF0 entry tramp (sta $1FF8 lands on the
    302  f0fc							; jmp below at $FEF3). Exits via `jmp MothExitPad` ($FC49): bank2 runs
    303  f0fc							; sta $1FF6, bank0 serves jmp UE_Next. Rules:
    304  f0fc							;   - NEVER jsr FoldIndirect or any bank0 routine (a fold from inside
    305  f0fc							;     bank2 would switch away mid-routine = frozen player).
    306  f0fc							;   - Enemy records ARE here (org $F9D9) — read directly, no fold needed.
    307  f0fc							;   - Keep the whole routine inline (no jsr): tramps are tail jmps so
    308  f0fc							;     the stack depth equals the UE body (+0 vs the $F8 guard).
    309  f0fc							;   - ZP (rect cache, EnemyRam*, EnemyDataLo/Hi) is RAM: bank-independent.
    310  f100					      org	$F100
    311  f100				   MothRoutine
    312  f100							; E4 Stage C: horizontal patrol (docs/e4_moth_plan.md). 1 px / 2 frames
    313  f100							; (EnemyRamP & 1), range = spawn ± 8 tiles (32 px), wall/range/wrap =
    314  f100							; flip dir + hold, clear = commit candidate. Row/col inputs feed a
    315  f100							; verbatim copy of PlayerHitsMap's P3.4 rect walk; HIT turns instead of
    316  f100							; returning C=1.
    317  f100							; In: X = slot, Y = record base, FetchPtr = record base (records are in
    318  f100							; THIS bank — direct (FetchPtr),Y reads, NO fold). NEVER jsr bank0
    319  f100							; (mid-bank2 fold = frozen player). Slot is saved to EnemyIndex because
    320  f100							; the col swap and walk both use X (E3 lesson). Every exit re-stages
    321  f100							; FetchPtr (the walk overwrites it with window bytes) then
    322  f100							; jmp MothExitPad (sta $1FF6 / jmp UE_Next in bank0).
    323  f100		       a5 c2		      lda	EnemyRamP
    324  f102		       29 01		      and	#1
